@*
    The gallery's full-size view, hosted by Radzen's DialogService.

    WHY RADZEN HERE, when almost nothing else in this app uses it. The previous version
    was a hand-rolled `div[role=dialog][aria-modal=true]` — correct roles, and nothing
    behind them: Escape did not close it, focus was never moved into it, Tab walked
    straight out into the page underneath, and closing left focus wherever it had been.
    That is the failure mode a modal dialog exists to prevent, and it is not a styling
    problem, so re-skinning would not have fixed it.

    DialogService brings the focus trap, the Escape handler, the inert backdrop and the
    focus restore. What it does NOT bring is a look — `.rz-dialog` is restyled onto the
    flap surfaces in app.css's overrides layer, so the board is unchanged.

    The rule this follows, and the reason the rest of the app still hand-rolls its
    surfaces: adopt a component library for BEHAVIOUR that is hard to get right, never
    for appearance this design system already owns.
*@
<div class="gallery-lightbox__panel">
    <img class="gallery-lightbox__img" src="@Item.ImageUrl" alt="@Item.FileName" />

    <div class="gallery-lightbox__meta">
        <span class="gallery-lightbox__name">
            <i class="bi @IconClass me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>@Item.FileName
        </span>
        <span class="gallery-lightbox__sub">
            @Item.Kind · @FormatSize(Item.SizeBytes) · @Item.CreatedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("g")
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="gallery-lightbox__actions">
        <button class="flap-btn flap-btn--primary flap-btn--sm" @onclick="@(() => Dialog.Close(LightboxResult.Use))">
            <i class="bi bi-check2 me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Use this image
        </button>
        <button class="flap-btn flap-btn--sm" @onclick="@(() => Dialog.Close(LightboxResult.Download))">
            <i class="bi bi-download me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Download
        </button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the viewer asked for on the way out. Null when they simply dismissed.</summary>
    public enum LightboxResult { Use, Download }

    [Inject] private DialogService Dialog { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public MyImagesGallery.GalleryItem Item { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Bootstrap-icon class for the kind badge, passed in so the mapping stays in one place.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string IconClass { get; set; } = "bi-image";

    private static string FormatSize(long bytes) =>
        bytes >= 1024 * 1024 ? $"{bytes / 1024.0 / 1024.0:0.#} MB" : $"{bytes / 1024.0:0} KB";
}
